  "detail": "`parseRepos` throws `Unknown repos key` for anything other than `discreet` and `branch_prefix`, so the daemon refuses to start. #687 (in review) adds `land_requires_approval` to the same `[repos.\"<owner>/<name>\"]` table with its own parser. Whichever lands second conflicts, and with this parser a config that sets `land_requires_approval` stops the daemon. More generally, after any release adds a repository key, rolling back to this release refuses to start (AGENTS.md: 'Leave the previous release working'; 'If an older release would refuse to start with a new key set, say so in the docs'). Required: ignore unknown `[repos.*]` keys with a warning instead of refusing to start, keep strict type checks for the keys this release knows, and put the repository-settings parser in one place both features use (`repoSettings`). Test: an unknown key loads with a warning."
